{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When your document gets large, you can split it up into subdocuments for easier editing."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= My book\n\ninclude::chapter01.adoc[]\n\ninclude::chapter02.adoc[]\n\ninclude::chapter03.adoc[]"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note the empty lines before and after the include directives. This practice is recommended whenever including AsciiDoc content to avoid unexpected results (e.g., a section title getting interpreted as a line at the end of a previous paragraph)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "leveloffset"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute can help here by pushing all headings in the included document down by the specified number of levels. This allows you to publish each chapter as a standalone document (complete with a document title), but still be able to include the chapters into a primary document (which has its own document title)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can easily assemble your book so that the chapter document titles become level 1 headings using:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= My Book\n\ninclude::chapter01.adoc[leveloffset=+1]\n\ninclude::chapter02.adoc[leveloffset=+1]\n\ninclude::chapter03.adoc[leveloffset=+1]"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Because the leveloffset is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "relative"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (it begins with + or -), this works even if the included document has its own includes and leveloffsets."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you have lots of chapters to include and want them all to have the same offset, you can save some typing by setting "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "leveloffset"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " around the includes:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= My book\n\n:leveloffset: +1\n\ninclude::chapter01.adoc[]\n\ninclude::chapter02.adoc[]\n\ninclude::chapter03.adoc[]\n\n:leveloffset: -1"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The final line returns the level offset to 0."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Alternatively, you could use absolute levels:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":leveloffset: 1\n\n//includes\n\n:leveloffset: 0"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Relative levels are preferred. Absolute levels become awkward when you have nested includes since they aren’t context aware."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_manipulate_heading_levels_with_leveloffset",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Manipulate heading levels with leveloffset"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Offset Section Levels"
      }
    ]
  }
}
